context:
GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/intel/asn/{asn}
Gets an overview of the Autonomous System Number (ASN) and a list of subnets for it.
Required: asn (path); account_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/intel/indicator-feeds/{feed_id}
Retrieves details for a specific custom threat indicator feed.
Required: account_id (path); feed_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/intel/indicator-feeds/{feed_id}/uploads/{upload_id}
Polls an asynchronously accepted upload. Continue polling after the recommended `poll_after_seconds` delay until status is `Unified` or `Error`. `Unified` is returned only after the durable loader finishes.
Required: account_id (path); feed_id (path); upload_id (path)

PUT /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/intel/indicator-feeds/{feed_id}
Revises details for a specific custom threat indicator feed.
Required: account_id (path); feed_id (path); body (body)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/intel/sinkholes/{sinkhole_id}
Delete the specified sinkhole. The sinkhole must not have any active ingress rules defined. A 409 response code indicates that this condition is not met.
Required: account_id (path) — The unique identifier for the Cloudflare account.; sinkhole_id (path) — The unique identifier for the sinkhole.

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/intel/sinkholes/{sinkhole_id}
Get the specified sinkhole by its unique identifier.
Required: account_id (path) — The unique identifier for the Cloudflare account.; sinkhole_id (path) — The unique identifier for the sinkhole.

PUT /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/intel/sinkholes/{sinkhole_id}
Replaces the name or R2 configuration of the specified sinkhole. This is a full replacement. All fields, including r2_secret, must be re-supplied. Omitting r2_secret overwrites the stored value with an empty string.
Required: account_id (path) — The unique identifier for the Cloudflare account.; sinkhole_id (path) — The unique identifier for the sinkhole.; body (body)
